TITLE:: Mapper
summary:: one controller mapper for every mixer, module and effect
categories:: Libraries>Mapper
related:: Classes/MapperMap, Classes/MapperTarget, Classes/MapperUnits, Classes/MapperWindow

DESCRIPTION::
A knob, fader or button of a controller on anything that says it can be moved - and on
several things at once, each with a range of its own.

code::
m = Mapper.default;
m.map(\m1, \kn_1_1, [\tidal, \bright], 0, 1);
m.map(\m1, \kn_1_1, [\tidal, \cut], 200, 4000, \exp);
m.code.postln;
m.gui;
::

Controllers come through the Modality toolkit (code::MKtl::), looked up by name: without it
there are no controllers, and a Tidal mapping still works, moved from code. The mapper depends
on nothing else, and nothing it maps depends on it.

subsection:: Targets

A target is named by an address, code::[provider, ... path]::, that stays the same across
rebuilds, reloads and sessions - see link::Classes/MapperTarget::. A mapping is between names:
one whose target is not there strong::waits::, and starts working when it comes back; one whose
controller is not there yet starts working when it is (looked at once a second).

An element may move several targets. A target has one element: mapping it again replaces the
mapping it had.

subsection:: Providers

Whoever has something to map registers under a key and answers two messages.

table::
## code::mapTargetAt(path):: || the description of one thing (an Event, see link::Classes/MapperTarget::), or nil
## code::mapTargets:: || the descriptions of everything it has now, each with its code::path::
## code::mapAddressOf(unit, key):: || optional: the path of a parameter of an effect it holds, so a knob in that effect's window can be learnt
## code::mapsSavedElsewhere:: || optional: true when its own sessions save its mappings, so the mapper's file leaves them out
## code::mapLabel:: || optional: what the window calls it
::

It says code::changed(\mapTargets):: when what it has changes. The mapper brings two providers
of its own: code::\tidal:: (code::[\tidal, name]:: is Tidal's cF "name") and code::\units::, a
link::Classes/MapperUnits::.

code::
(
~level = 0.5;
~provider = (
	mapTargetAt: { |self, path|
		if (path[0] == \level) {
			(path: [\level], label: "my level", spec: ControlSpec(0, 1),
				get: { ~level }, set: { |v| ~level = v })
		}
	},
	mapTargets: { |self| [self.mapTargetAt([\level])] }
);
Mapper.register(\mine, ~provider);
Mapper.default.targets.collect(_.address);
);
::

subsection:: Saving

The code is the storage. link::#*default:: reads link::#*defaultPath:: the first time it is asked
for and writes it a moment after a mapping changes, unless link::#*autoSave:: is false. The
mapper is never freed by cmd-period or a server reboot: it has nothing on the server.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: default
The mapper everything shares. Made, and its file read, the first time it is asked for.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Mapper::

METHOD:: new
A mapper of its own, with no file: for a test, or a set of mappings kept apart.

METHOD:: register
Put a provider on the shared mapper.
ARGUMENT:: key
a Symbol, the first item of its targets' addresses
ARGUMENT:: provider
anything that answers code::mapTargetAt:: and code::mapTargets::

METHOD:: unregister
Take a provider off the shared mapper. Its mappings stay, and wait.

METHOD:: units
The shared mapper's link::Classes/MapperUnits::.

METHOD:: isAvailable
Whether the Modality toolkit is installed.

METHOD:: defaultPath
The file link::#*default:: reads and writes.

METHOD:: autoLoad
Whether link::#*default:: reads its file when it is made.

METHOD:: autoSave
Whether it writes it by itself.

METHOD:: tidalPort
Where Tidal listens for controls, 6010.

METHOD:: codeOf
A value as you would type it.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: map
Map an element of a controller to a target.
ARGUMENT:: ktl
the MKtl's name
ARGUMENT:: element
the element's name in its description (code::\kn_1_1::); a note pair goes by its group's
ARGUMENT:: address
the target's
ARGUMENT:: lo
where the control's bottom sends it, in the target's own units; nil for the bottom of its range
ARGUMENT:: hi
the same for the top
ARGUMENT:: curve
code::\lin::, code::\exp::, code::\log::, code::\scurve::, a Number or an Env
ARGUMENT:: invert
turn the control round
ARGUMENT:: takeover
code::\pickup:: or code::\jump::
ARGUMENT:: mode
a button's: code::\toggle:: or code::\momentary::
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/MapperMap::, or nil when something else owns the target

METHOD:: unmap
Take away the mapping of a target.

METHOD:: unmapElement
Take away every mapping of an element.

METHOD:: remove
Take away one link::Classes/MapperMap::.

METHOD:: clear
Every mapping and every controller name.

METHOD:: clearProvider
The mappings of one provider only.

METHOD:: mapFor
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/MapperMap:: of a target, or nil

METHOD:: mapsOf
RETURNS:: the maps of an element

METHOD:: mapsOfProvider
RETURNS:: the maps onto one provider's targets

METHOD:: maps
Every mapping, a List of link::Classes/MapperMap::.

METHOD:: learn
The next element moved on any controller is mapped to this address: a knob as soon as it moves,
a button when pressed.
ARGUMENT:: address
the target's
ARGUMENT:: action
a Function given the new link::Classes/MapperMap::

METHOD:: cancelLearn
Stop waiting.

METHOD:: isLearning

METHOD:: armed
The link::Classes/MapperTarget:: waiting for a controller, or nil.

METHOD:: learnMode
While it is on, a click on anything that can be mapped arms it, in every window that follows the
mapper's code::\learnMode::.

METHOD:: register
Put a provider on this mapper.

METHOD:: unregister

METHOD:: providers
An IdentityDictionary, key to provider.

METHOD:: units
Its link::Classes/MapperUnits::.

METHOD:: targets
Everything that can be mapped now.
RETURNS:: an Array of link::Classes/MapperTarget::

METHOD:: addressOf
The address of a parameter of an effect some provider holds, or nil.

METHOD:: useKtl
Take mappings from an MKtl, making it from the description when there is none of that name.

METHOD:: forgetKtl
Stop listening to an MKtl. Its mappings go; the MKtl stays.

METHOD:: findDevices
Modality's MKtl.find.
RETURNS:: the devices seen

METHOD:: devices
The devices of the last find, an Event each.

METHOD:: connect
A found device on the mapper.

METHOD:: ktls
The controllers' names and descriptions.

METHOD:: ktl
The MKtl of a name.

METHOD:: ktlState
code::\connected::, code::\virtual:: or code::\missing::.

METHOD:: isButton
Whether an element is a button; nil when the controller is not there to ask.

METHOD:: sendTidal
Set a Tidal control.

METHOD:: tidalValues
What has been sent, by name.

METHOD:: code
The mappings as code that makes them again.
ARGUMENT:: all
true: also those a provider's own sessions save

METHOD:: save
Write the code to a file; its own link::#-path:: when none is given.

METHOD:: load
A file of mappings in place of the ones there are. A file that is not there clears them.

METHOD:: loadCode
Run mappings given as text.

METHOD:: path
Where it saves by itself, if anywhere.

METHOD:: gui
RETURNS:: its link::Classes/MapperWindow::

METHOD:: refreshFeedback
The LEDs of buttons on on/off targets, again.

METHOD:: free
Stop listening to every controller and provider.
